-- title:
--   Faithful flatness over the generic corner B/(f)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a local principal ideal domain with fraction field $K$ of characteristic $0$, let $H$ be a commutative Hopf $R$-algebra that is of finite type as an $R$-algebra, flat as an $R$-module and cocommutative, and with $K \otimes_R H$ finite over $K$, and let $H'$ be a commutative Hopf $R$-algebra, flat over $R$. Let $qc : H \to H'$ be a surjective bialgebra homomorphism, and write $B = \mathrm{hopfKer}(qc)$ for the $R$-subalgebra of $H$ consisting of the $a$ with $(\mathrm{id}_H \otimes qc)(\Delta a) = a \otimes 1$ in $H \otimes_R H'$. Assume given idempotents $e \in H$ and $e' \in H'$ such that the localisations $H_e$ and $H'_{e'}$ are finite as $R$-modules while the maximal ideal of $R$ generates the unit ideal in $H_{1-e}$ and in $H'_{1-e'}$, and such that $qc(e) = e'$. Assume further that $f \in H$ is an idempotent lying in $B$, with $fe = e$, and minimal in the sense that every $b \in B$ with $be = 0$ satisfies $bf = 0$. The conclusion is that $(B/(f)) \otimes_B H$ is a faithfully flat module over $B/(f)$, the quotient of $B$ by the ideal generated by $f$.
--
--   In the geometric reading, $\mathrm{Spec}\,H$ is a quasi-finite flat commutative group scheme $G$ over the local base $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$, $\mathrm{Spec}\,H'$ a flat closed subgroup $N$, $B$ the ring of $N$-invariants, and $f$ the idempotent cutting out the $N$-orbit of the finite part of $G$; the statement treats the corner of $B$ complementary to $f$, where the uniformiser of $R$ is invertible, so that everything takes place over $K$. It is one of the two corner computations feeding [`HopfAlgebra.faithfullyFlat_hopfKer_of_finitePartIdempotent`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.faithfullyFlat_hopfKer_of_finitePartIdempotent), the faithful flatness of $H$ over the $N$-invariants (equivalently, flatness of the quotient map $G \to G/N$) in the local split quasi-finite case.
